# Ultron — how git should treat this tree.
#
# This project has been bitten by line endings more than once: several modules
# are CRLF, several are LF, and a patch tool that reads bytes has to ask which.
# Recording the answer here stops git from rewriting one into the other on
# Windows and also stops a diff from showing a whole file as changed because of
# an invisible carriage return.
#
# The rule: Python and Markdown are LF everywhere. Windows launchers are CRLF,
# because cmd.exe and PowerShell read them and a lone LF in a .bat file is a
# broken file on some Windows versions.

* text=auto eol=lf

*.py    text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf
*.txt   text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf
*.yml   text eol=lf

*.bat   text eol=crlf
*.cmd   text eol=crlf
*.ps1   text eol=crlf

# Real binaries. Never diffed, never converted.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.gif binary
*.webm binary
*.mp4 binary
*.zip binary
